# Browser
# Bot1's page shows what Old Man of the Sea's control effect is: the Llanowar Elves it took says on its face who controls
# it, for how long and why - "You control it for as long as Old Man of the Sea remains tapped and its power
# remains less than or equal to Old Man of the Sea's power" (CR 611.2b, 613.1b). In Bot1's next untap step the page asks
# "Old Man of the Sea: untap it during this untap step?" (CR 502.3), and Bot1 leaves it tapped, keeping the Elves.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Island
Old Man of the Sea
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Old Man of the Sea.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Old Man of the Sea.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Client.Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Rules = {T}: Add {G}. / You control it for as long as Old Man of the Sea remains tapped and its power remains less than or equal to Old Man of the Sea's power (Old Man of the Sea).
[T4 Bot2.End]
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Old Man of the Sea: untap it during this untap step?
Bot1.Decline
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Old Man of the Sea.Tapped = true

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet; Island; Old Man of the Sea; Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Battlefield.Old Man of the Sea.Tapped = true
